Third-party components
- Jackson (jackson-core, jackson-databind, Apache-2.0) is shaded into the Bukkit agent as
  io.github.h7kz.proofstone.shaded.jackson. Its upstream LICENSE and NOTICE texts must travel with that jar.
- Bedrock driver host jar (drivers/bedrock, ADR-0018 and ADR-0021), shaded and relocated, never in a user's dependency graph:
  - CloudburstMC Protocol and Netty transports (org.cloudburstmc.*, Apache-2.0), including netty-transport-nethernet.
  - Netty (Apache-2.0), Gson (Apache-2.0), Jackson (Apache-2.0), Bouncy Castle (MIT-style licence), jose4j (Apache-2.0).
  - libdatachannel-java (the Java binding, MIT per its POM) and the native libraries inside it, libdatachannel and libjuice,
    which are MPL-2.0 (ADR-0011 amendment, T-M12-08). They are shipped unmodified, as the OpenCollab build
    dev.opencollab:libdatachannel-java:0.24.6.0-20261105.085043-11 made them (linux-glibc-x86_64 and linux-glibc-aarch64), from
    libdatachannel revision 2e2d86acc27a4734db2f28f95d09c1ab7a83836f and libjuice revision 67bfe8903b8d6a5dcf8d731271aec68257cb2872
    (read from the jar's MANIFEST). The binding's classes stay under their own package name because the native code is bound to it.
    MPL-2.0 text: https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. Source of libdatachannel: https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libdatachannel,
    of libjuice: https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libjuice, of the binding and the build: https://github.com/opencollab-incubator/libdatachannel-java.
- Other dependencies are either test-only or not redistributed. Their licences are listed in
  docs/adr/0011-licensing.md and docs/release-notes-0.1.0.md.
- ViaProxy (GPL-3.0) runs only as a separate, unmodified container image. It is not redistributed.
- The Paper and Spigot APIs are compile-only and not redistributed.
